  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The prayer over the chalice, said as the priest raises it. Its own document because it accompanies the second of the two offerings and closes with its own Amen; the two prayers that follow it are said over gifts already on the corporal and are carried together at ordinarium.in-spiritu-humilitatis. SALUTÁRIS at w005 is the genitive singular of the neuter noun salutáre, the corpus lemma at ordinarium.iudica-me w089 and ordinarium.deus-tu-conversus w018, not the adjective salutáris agreeing with cálicem — the case of cálicem is accusative and would not admit it. DEPRECÁNTES at w007 is nominative plural masculine, agreeing with the unwritten subject of Offérimus; the form is also accusative and vocative. NOSTRA at w016 is ablative singular feminine agreeing with salúte across four words, not the neuter plural the same spelling would allow.",
    "source": {
